#
# What energy costs at a tariff (understory_rules.h UR1), in Sutra: mj
# millijoules at tariff minor units of the owner's currency per kWh (one
# kWh is 3600000000 mJ), floor(mj * tariff / 3600000000), never rounded
# up. mj fits 9(12) (about 277 kWh) and tariff 9(6), so a larger or a
# negative one is a size error: refused. cost.cpp says the same in C++
# (as WebAssembly), which answers to 64 bits: past the pictures the two
# disagree and the cost is held. Advice only: it is no bill.
record energy-cost
  mj: 9(12)
  tariff: 9(6)
  cost: 9(9)
procedure
  compute cost = mj * tariff / 3600000000
  answer cost
